cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Reflexive Thematic Analysis Canvas in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Reflexive Thematic Analysis Canvas: A browser-only workspace for reflexive thematic analysis of qualitative text data"
version: "0.9.0"
abstract: "A zero-backend browser workspace for reflexive thematic analysis (Braun & Clarke) of interview transcripts, focus groups and open-ended survey answers (.txt, .csv, .docx, .doc, REFI-QDA .qdpx). Supports overlapping coding, full-text search with a separate speaker layer, a theme board with review and definition status, an automatic audit trail with a reflexive journal, and Word (.docx) export of write-up tables. Data stays in the browser and no AI is used. An independent project, not affiliated with Virginia Braun or Victoria Clarke."
authors:
